The C++ BPM kernels were translated from the accompanying Python port of
the original Fortran expressions. Driver auxiliaries and the TNO integration
were implemented in C++. The original empirical expressions, switches and
fixed 61-point quadrature are retained; this work does not add a new noise model.

reference/fortran/dqk61.f contains SLATEC/QUADPACK's 61-point Gauss-Kronrod
routine, used as a developer validation reference; its original provenance
comments are preserved. Intel oneMKL and the compiler are external dependencies
and are not redistributed in this repository.
